sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/task-containers.md): on a host with `settings.task_vms.containers`, a task start that gets a container place copies the host's base container snapshot instead of the base VM snapshot. The workflow and its step names stay those of docs/cli/task/start.mmd; the intent carries `runtime: container`, and the Ansible parts branch on it. The container keeps the task VM's Node identity until ADR 0250 step 6 (a temporary exception that ADR 0250 records).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:start
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane TC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve · Swamp Node
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  participant TC as Task container<br/>HOST-tvm-N
  Note over GW: Claim a task place<br/>mint an identity · database only
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `task:start` for a todo group, a proof, a build, a fix turn or a review round
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a host with `settings.task_vms.containers`, a free container place in the pool the request uses, and a base container snapshot that a refresh promoted on that host
  %%> - `task_vms.container_placement` on, or the request is the host's container refresh proof or an operator `proof:run --host`; until the switch, normal work goes to task VMs
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the same records as a task VM start: the slot `HOST-tvm-N`, the Node with its `app-dev` role, a WireGuard key pair in the reserved range, the agent secret and an SSH host key, pinned on the Node
  %%> - the claim's Pi token and Pi models file in the vault; the models file holds the model router guard origin and the one fixed model key
  %%> - the intent records `runtime: container`; the row keeps it, so the release and the sweep take the same path later
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-provision
  SW->>TC: Start and converge<br/>one Ansible run
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `ansible-playbook` run, two parts, as for a task VM
  %%> - host part on the container host: `incus copy` of the base container's recorded snapshot to `HOST-tvm-N` (a ZFS clone, about 0.5 s); the copy carries the inner Incus with the nested fleet and its `base` snapshots in the inner directory pool, so there is no seed volume to clone
  %%> - it pushes the identity and the claim into the stopped copy with `incus file push` from stdin: the WireGuard key and config, the SSH host key, the agent secret and config, the Pi unit, token and models file; no identity volume and no boot unit that applies one
  %%> - the base enables the tunnel, the agent and the Pi unit with `ConditionPathExists=` on their identity files, so they start at the copy's first boot; Incus sets the hostname from the container's name
  %%> - it refuses a copy with any device beyond its root disk and NIC or any `raw.*` key, sets `limits.cpu`, `limits.memory`, the root disk size of the place and `boot.autostart=true`, then `incus start`; the outer container boots in about a second, and the nested containers start by themselves
  %%> - converge part over WireGuard: the converge of the release refresh, a no-op on a current base, then the new task branch on the warm checkout; it waits up to 300 s for SSH, polling every second
  %%> Pi:
  %%> - the Pi server binary is in the base; the start only writes the claim's token and models file, and starts the Pi unit on the container's WireGuard address
  SW->>HUB: Add the hub peer<br/>peer file · wg addconf
  %%> Runs beside the step before it: Swamp starts both at once.
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the container's public key and address on the WireGuard hub; the container's own tunnel goes out through the host bridge as UDP to the hub's public endpoint
  SW->>TC: Reach the VM by WireGuard<br/>ssh from Swamp · pinned key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the path every later step takes (sync, check, turn, script, proof): ssh from a Swamp worker to the container's WireGuard address with its pinned host key; the step keeps its VM name, because the workflow is shared
  %%> Workspace:
  %%> - the workspace has no steps of its own here: the warm checkout comes with the base, the task branch with the converge, and the Project setup with the baseline check, all over this path
  SW->>TC: Check ready<br/>one exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `incus exec` through the host: the agent, the tunnel unit `orbit-wireguard.service`, the Pi unit, a handshake on the interface `orbit` (`wg show orbit`), and the three nested containers `RUNNING`; Swamp's `assert` decides
  %%> - the tunnel unit comes from the intent (`slot.tunnel_unit`), so the step is the same for both runtimes
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>ready
    Note over GW: Record the container ready<br/>target under 20 s
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the group runs on its task container; Doctor, `vm_power` and the stray report treat it as they treat a task VM
    %%> Target:
    %%> - under 20 s from admission: copy 1 s, start and nested autostart under 10 s, a no-op converge about 6 s; the build PR measures it
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the release runs: the container, the hub peer, the keys and the Node record go, and the place is free
  end
